{{also|Sterben}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|sterban|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*sterbaną}}, itself either from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*(s)terp-||to lose force; lose sensibility, become numb; be dead, be motionless}} or from {{term/t|ine-pro|*sterbʰ-||to be stiff, become stiff}}. Cognate with Low German {{term|starven|lang=nds}}, {{term|staarven|lang=nds}}, Dutch {{term|sterven|lang=nl}}, West Frisian {{term|stjerre|lang=fy}}, English {{term|starve|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈʃtɛʁbm̩]|lang=de}}
* {{hyphenation|ster|ben}}
* {{audio|De-sterben.ogg|audio (Germany)}}
* {{audio|De-at-sterben.ogg|audio (Austria)}}

